MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f2f9ec81392f3254b96fef70765aaae9, type: 3}
  m_Name: Debrief_COC1
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::CircuitCrafter.Assessment.ModuleDebriefData
  moduleId: COC1
  headline: "It came in as a box of parts and it's going out as a working machine
    \u2014 that's the whole job in one sentence. Here's what the run showed about
    how you work."
  practiceNotice: 
  assessorNotes:
  - outcomeCode: "LO1 \xB7 Assemble computer hardware"
    assessorLooksFor: "An assessor watches the order you work in and how you handle
      the boards \u2014 strap on before the case is open, CPU seated and its retention
      arm fully down before the cooler goes on, RAM clipped at both ends. That the
      machine starts afterwards is not the evidence; how you got there is."
  - outcomeCode: "LO2 \xB7 Prepare installer"
    assessorLooksFor: 'You are watched for whether you verify the installer before
      you trust it: the right image for the architecture, a drive you have confirmed
      is bootable, and no assumption that last term''s USB is still good.'
  - outcomeCode: "LO3 \xB7 Install operating system and drivers for peripherals/devices"
    assessorLooksFor: "An assessor looks for drivers from a known source in a sensible
      order, and for you checking Device Manager for anything left unrecognised \u2014
      rather than declaring it done when the desktop appears."
  - outcomeCode: "LO4 \xB7 Install application software"
    assessorLooksFor: The check is licensing and fitness for purpose, not speed.
      Install what the job sheet asks for, from media you can account for, and confirm
      each one actually launches.
  - outcomeCode: "LO5 \xB7 Conduct testing and documentation"
    assessorLooksFor: "This is the outcome most learners lose. Test against the specification
      and write down what you did \u2014 serials, what was installed, what you replaced.
      Work with no record is work nobody can verify."
  nextButtonLabel: Take the assessment
  nextSceneName: 
  nextButtonLabelAfterAssessment: 
  nextSceneNameAfterAssessment: 
  replayButtonLabel: Run it again
